{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01N1:proof", "parent_tag": "01MX", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "By Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>\nwe may replace <MATH_0001> by the image of <MATH_0002>\nwithout changing <MATH_0003> or the sheaves <MATH_0004>.\nThus we may assume that <MATH_0005> is surjective. By\nLemma <REF_0003> we get (1) and (2)\nand surjectivity in (3).\nBy Lemma <REF_0004> we see that both\n<MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007>\nare invertible. Hence <MATH_0008> is an isomorphism.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-eventual-iso-graded-rings-map-proj}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-morphism-proj-transitive}", "MATH_0001": "$B$", "MATH_0002": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(n)$", "MATH_0005": "$A \\to B$", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-surjective-graded-rings-map-proj}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-apply-modules}", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(n)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y(n)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\theta$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:f203ff4f05f0774c58830ef86a3dc6d931e4ddb527db9937d47f967e7cf1f40e", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:95d30ac7bb9d3fd55f4fa803e7b542f036ba4d9cef91b4422b9e57576e8460fa", "source_math_hash": "sha256:73166c2bae53ab5f21d65d9ead8c4b01e09d59ce3757367695b6e2ab145fb74e"}
